<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 rises 1.02 pct, M2 up 1.5 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 rises 1.02 pct, M2 up 1.5 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 700.8 billion levs on May 16 from 693.7 billion levs a week earlier and M2 edged up to 3,276.4 billion levs from 3,227.9 billion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 2.06 percent to 3,468.3 billion levs in the week to May 16.</p>
<p>Conversion of dollar-denominated deposits into levs was made at the central bank fixings of 1,511.4 levs per dollar for May 16, 1,499.4 for May 9 and 1,467.8 for April 25.</p>
